slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

doc{$title"Links and navigation"
  t.lead"Anything can be a link: a piece of text, a button, an image or a whole box. The `to` attribute says where it goes."
  section{$id"kinds" $title"Kinds of links"
    demo{$code"text { \"Read the \" link(to: \"text.slml\") \"text chapter\" \".\" }\nrow(gap: 12) {\n  button(to: \"#targets\") \"A button\"\n  image(src: \"/logo.png\", alt: \"Home\", width: 40, to: \"/index.slml\")\n}\ncolumn(to: \"/layout-guide.slml\", fill: #f4f4f8, padding: 14, radius: 10) {\n  text(bold: true) \"A whole box is a link\"\n  text \"Click anywhere in it.\"\n}"
      "Read the [text chapter](text.slml)."
      r{g12
        btn{>#targets "A button"}
        img{/logo.png w40 >/index.slml "Home"}
      }
      c{>/layout-guide.slml bg#f4f4f8 p14 r10
        t{b "A whole box is a link"}
        "Click anywhere in it."
      }
    }
    warning{$title"No links inside links"
      "A link, button or linked box can't contain another link, button or form field. In HTML this is a common source of broken pages; in SLML it is an error."
    }
  }
  section{$id"targets" $title"Where a link can go"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"about.slml" $values"a page" $about"Relative to the current file. Compiled sites link to about.html automatically."}
      ref{$name"/docs/a.slml" $values"from the root" $about"A leading slash starts at the site root, so the link works from any folder."}
      ref{$name"#contact" $values"an anchor" $about"An element on this page with id: \"contact\". It must exist."}
      ref{$name"a.slml#top" $values"page + anchor" $about"A place on another page."}
      ref{$name"https://…" $values"a website" $about"Also http:, mailto: (e-mail) and tel: (phone). Other schemes are rejected."}
    }
    "Paths can't contain `..`. To reach a parent folder, start at the root with `/`. This keeps every link inside your site."
    "Write local file names literally: `reports/annual report 100%.pdf` or `żółć.slml`. The compiler handles spaces, Unicode and URL escaping for you. Do not replace a space with `%20` in an SLML file path; that would mean a file whose name contains the characters %20. External URLs keep their usual escaping."
    note{$title"Broken links are errors"
      "When you compile or check a page, every link to a file in your site is checked. A typo in a file name is reported like any other mistake, before your visitors find it."
    }
  }
  section{$id"anchors" $title"Anchors"
    "Give any block element an `id`, then link to it with `#`. Ids start with a letter and must be unique on the page."
    code"""
        text { link(to: "#faq") "Jump to the questions" }
        ...
        heading(level: 2, id: "faq") "Questions"
        """
    "The chapter headings of this handbook are anchors: try [this link](#kinds)."
  }
  section{$id"navigation" $title"Site navigation"
    "A menu is a row of links. To show the same menu on every page, put it in a [component](/components.slml) in a shared file:"
    code"""
        // parts.slml
        slml 0.1

        define menu {
          row(gap: 20, padding: 16, align: center) {
            text(bold: true) { link(to: "/index.slml") "My site" }
            spacer
            text { link(to: "/blog/index.slml") "Blog" }
            text { link(to: "/contact.slml") "Contact" }
          }
        }
        """
    code"""
        // any page, in any folder
        slml 0.1
        use "/parts.slml"

        page { menu  heading "Welcome" }
        """
  }
  pager{$prev"/content.slml" $prev-label"Lists, code and images" $next"/components.slml" $next-label"Components and imports"}
}
